WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.958
Morning, Ziad.

00:00:00.958 --> 00:00:02.396
Friday the twentieth.

00:00:02.396 --> 00:00:08.076
A warm, sunny one, with a short work block on the calendar and a late plan tonight.

00:00:08.076 --> 00:00:10.609
Here's one to chew on while you move.

00:00:10.609 --> 00:00:17.796
With a two to one compressor, if a sound goes four steps over the threshold, how many steps come through?

00:00:17.796 --> 00:00:19.165
Answer's at the end.

00:00:19.165 --> 00:00:20.602
Weather's easy today.

00:00:20.602 --> 00:00:27.241
Sunny and dry, mid-forties now, up to the upper sixties by early afternoon, with barely a breeze.

00:00:27.241 --> 00:00:38.261
Saturday stays dry too, but a coastal storm could bring heavy rain and wind from late Sunday into Monday, and then it turns sharply colder ahead of Thanksgiving.

00:00:38.261 --> 00:00:39.219
Okay, the day.

00:00:39.219 --> 00:00:42.299
Calendar has the gym at seven, straight sets.

00:00:42.299 --> 00:00:44.557
Then work from home, nine to one.

00:00:44.557 --> 00:00:49.075
There's a video call on there at one-thirty, just fifteen minutes.

00:00:49.075 --> 00:00:51.470
And plans on there at nine tonight.

00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:57.630
So the whole afternoon and early evening are open, on maybe the last warm day for a while.

00:00:57.630 --> 00:00:58.589
Alright, news.

00:00:58.589 --> 00:00:59.958
The big money story.

00:00:59.958 --> 00:01:02.285
Anthropic went public on Thursday.

00:01:02.285 --> 00:01:10.361
Shares priced at eighty-three dollars, above the range it had pitched, and it raised about eighty-one billion dollars.

00:01:10.361 --> 00:01:14.605
That puts the whole company at around one and a half trillion.

00:01:14.605 --> 00:01:17.069
It trades on the Nasdaq under A.N.T.

00:01:17.069 --> 00:01:24.118
It's one of the biggest stock debuts ever, and it's a real test of how much people will pay for an A.I.

00:01:24.118 --> 00:01:26.240
lab before the profits show up.

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:27.678
One from your corner.

00:01:27.678 --> 00:01:31.716
Ideogram put out version four point six of its image model.

00:01:31.716 --> 00:01:41.093
It now makes images at full four K, and it's better at precise edits, where you change one thing and leave the rest of the picture alone.

00:01:41.093 --> 00:01:46.226
Ideogram says it's now first on a leaderboard for multi-step image editing.

00:01:46.226 --> 00:01:50.264
That claim's only from Ideogram so far, so take it loosely.

00:01:50.264 --> 00:01:52.865
And the summit in Shenzhen wrapped up.

00:01:52.865 --> 00:01:57.383
Trump, Xi, and Putin put out what they called a peace declaration.

00:01:57.383 --> 00:02:06.349
They agreed a nuclear war can't be won and must never be fought, and promised to keep talking about nuclear risk, with no timeline.

00:02:06.349 --> 00:02:12.098
There was nothing about actually cutting weapons, and nothing about Ukraine or Iran.

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:15.726
Putin said himself that nobody's forced to follow it.

00:02:15.726 --> 00:02:17.368
So it's mostly symbolic.

00:02:17.368 --> 00:02:22.228
Okay, here's one for next week, or Sunday night once the rain comes in.

00:02:22.228 --> 00:02:28.799
There's a new movie theater on Troutman Street, near Knickerbocker, that only plays short films.

00:02:28.799 --> 00:02:31.194
It's in the old Mad Tropical space.

00:02:31.194 --> 00:02:37.080
One screen in the back, a late-night cafe up front, and the lineup changes every week.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:43.309
You pay by how many shorts you watch, and the owner says nothing costs more than ten bucks.

00:02:43.309 --> 00:02:46.457
No bar, though, so it's coffee, not cocktails.

00:02:46.457 --> 00:02:48.785
Today's challenge is a making one.

00:02:48.785 --> 00:02:52.207
Fix one small broken thing at home this afternoon.

00:02:52.207 --> 00:02:57.819
A loose cabinet hinge, a wobbly chair leg, a button that's hanging on by a thread.

00:02:57.819 --> 00:03:01.310
Pick the one you've been stepping around for weeks.

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:03.979
Ten minutes, whatever tools you've got.

00:03:03.979 --> 00:03:09.386
It's a small win, and it clears a tiny bit of background noise from your place.

00:03:09.386 --> 00:03:11.919
Okay, something you've been learning.

00:03:11.919 --> 00:03:17.189
Remember wiring up the memo so a push renders the audio and updates the feed?

00:03:17.189 --> 00:03:21.638
Today's what actually happens in the few minutes after that push.

00:03:21.638 --> 00:03:25.197
First, GitHub hands the job to a brand new computer.

00:03:25.197 --> 00:03:28.072
Not a server that's sitting there waiting.

00:03:28.072 --> 00:03:33.684
A fresh, empty Linux machine, made just for this run, and thrown away right after.

00:03:33.684 --> 00:03:39.639
That's why the memo's recipe installs the audio tool from scratch every single morning.

00:03:39.639 --> 00:03:42.103
Nothing carries over from yesterday.

00:03:42.103 --> 00:03:43.198
Second, the key.

00:03:43.198 --> 00:03:46.210
The voice service key is stored as a secret.

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:52.506
The machine can use it, but if it ever shows up in the log, GitHub blanks it out with stars.

00:03:52.506 --> 00:04:00.446
And the recipe checks the key is there before doing any real work, so a missing key fails fast, not halfway through.

00:04:00.446 --> 00:04:01.610
Third, a line up.

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:04.827
The recipe says only one render runs at a time.

00:04:04.827 --> 00:04:11.192
If two pushes land close together, the second one waits its turn instead of racing the first.

00:04:11.192 --> 00:04:16.394
Otherwise two runs could both try to save the feed and trip over each other.

00:04:16.394 --> 00:04:17.215
Last, Pages.

00:04:17.215 --> 00:04:23.170
The finished folder, the audio and the feed, gets packed up and handed to GitHub Pages.

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:24.949
Pages is just a file host.

00:04:24.949 --> 00:04:26.250
No code runs there.

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:33.094
It serves copies through servers all over the world, and those copies can hang on for a few minutes.

00:04:33.094 --> 00:04:37.338
So a new episode can be live and still not show up right away.

00:04:37.338 --> 00:04:43.703
So: calendar says gym at seven, work till one, a quick call at one-thirty, and plans at nine.

00:04:43.703 --> 00:04:45.140
Fix one broken thing.

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:48.289
The answer: two steps, half of what went over.

00:04:48.289 --> 00:04:50.000
Have a good Friday, Ziad.
